
AMISOR borehole AM06 MICROCAT data for 2011/2012 season
-------------------------------------------------------

Data from the first download.

ascii format
------------
contained in column formatted files catxxxx_2.dat, where
xxxx = microcat serial number. The columns are:

1. decimal time - decimal days, where 0.0 = 0000 on January 1st 2001.
So, for example, midday on 15th January 2001 is decimal time 14.5
2. temperature (deg. C, T90)
3. conductivity (mS/cm)
4. pressure (dbar)
5. salinity (PSS78)
6. to 11. day, month, year, hour, minute, second.

* Note that all times are UTC.

* There is a line of data for each recording interval (i.e. no gaps),
and null data is represented by -999.0

* Clock errors were small (< 20 seconds), and no clock drift corrections have 
been made.

* Mean pressures over this latest download:

cat7325 =  552.2 dbar
cat7324 =  680.1 dbar
cat7323 =  790.2 dbar


* Original pressure data for microcat 7325 are suspect, with a steady drift of
~15 dbar over the year (continuing on from the drift during the previous year).
This drift not evident in the other 2 microcats. This pressure
trend was removed from the data (with an additional correction to set pressures
to the original value immediately after deployment in January 2010), and 
conductivity/salinity values recalculated.

Note that interpretation of this drifting pressure data is difficult. If the initial
pressure after deployment in January 2010 is believed, errors of the order 2 dbar might remain
in the current year's data (equivalent to salinity errors of ~0.002). 

The original uncorrected data are in the files cat7325_2uncorrected.dat and
cat7325_2uncorrected.mat.

Data calculated using a constant pressure value of 551.3 dbar (from immediately after
deployment in January 2010) are in the files cat7325_2meanp.dat and
cat7325_2meanp.mat.


matlab
------
contained in matlab format files catxxxx_2.mat, where
xxxx = microcat serial number. 



